      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. the tone is definitely better and more reassuring. i'm still seeing a lot of \"heavy\" words like \"incident\" and \"distress\" in there that are pulling the sentiment score down. \n\nthe board really wants to see a version that focuses on our commitment to excellence and how we're turning this into a positive step for our safety protocols. can you try one more version? just try to lean more into the \"proactive excellence\" and \"hospitality\" side of things. if we can get that positivity score closer to the 0.8-0.9 range, it'll make the meeting go way smoother. just try to keep the core facts about the investigation in there somewhere though.",
